      "answer": "Here is the **Poison** condition for Gloomhaven (2nd Edition), based on verified sources:\n\n---\n\n## Poison\n\n> **Poison:** All attacks targeting the figure gain \"+1 [Attack Modifier draw].\" Poison is removed when the figure is healed but, unlike *Wound*, Poison prevents the heal from increasing the figure's current hit point value.\n\n*(Gloomhaven 2e Rulebook, Negative Conditions section)*\n\n---\n\n### Key clarifications (from the official FAQ)\n\n- **Not stackable:** If multiple sources would apply *Poison* to the same figure from a single attack, it is still only one instance of *Poison*. A single *Safeguard* can still block it entirely.\n- **Objectives are immune:** Objectives cannot ever gain *Poison* (or any other condition).\n- **Allies with immunity:** You can attempt to give *Poison* to an allied figure that is immune to it; the condition simply doesn't apply.\n- **Bonus triggers on fulfillment:** If your card grants a bonus for giving an ally *Poison*, you earn that bonus even if the ally prevents the condition (e.g., via *Safeguard*).\n- **Sequential targeting:** *Poison* applied mid-ability (e.g., via an attack modifier card) takes effect before the next target is selected, consistent with Gloomhaven's sequential targeting rules.",
