      "answer": "Here is what **Poison** does in Gloomhaven (2nd Edition), straight from the rulebook:\n\n> **Poison:** All attacks targeting the figure gain \"+1 [attack modifier draw].\" Poison is removed when the figure is healed but, unlike wound, poison prevents the heal from increasing the figure's current hit point value.\n\n**In plain terms:**\n\n- Any attacker targeting a *Poisoned* figure draws an extra attack modifier card (the +1 modifier).\n- *Poison* is removed when the figure receives a *Heal* — but that healing does **not** restore any hit points. The condition is cleansed, but the HP benefit is lost.\n\n*(Gloomhaven 2e Rulebook, Negative Conditions)*",
