      "answer": "Here is what *Wound* does in Frosthaven, directly from the rulebook:\n\n> **Wound:** The figure suffers 1 damage at the start of each of their turns. Wound is removed when the figure is healed.\n\n**Key details from the same verified results:**\n\n- A single *Heal* can remove *Wound* (along with *Brittle* and *Bane*). However, if *Poison* is also present, the hit point increase from the heal is prevented (though *Wound* is still removed).\n- If a figure has both *Regenerate* and *Wound*, *Regenerate* is applied first — performing \"Heal 1, self\" at the start of the turn — which removes *Wound* before it deals its 1 damage.\n- *Wound* cannot be removed voluntarily; only a heal effect triggers its removal.\n- A figure cannot have multiple instances of *Wound*, but if it gains *Wound* again while already wounded, the duration resets.\n\n**Source:** Frosthaven Rulebook, passage 100 (Negative Conditions).",
