      "agentRuntime": "langgraph",
      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here is what *Poison* does in Frosthaven, from the rulebook:\n\n> **Poison:** All attacks targeting the figure gain \"+1 Attack.\" Poison is removed when the figure is healed but, unlike wound/brittle/bane, poison prevents the heal from increasing the figure's current hit point value.\n\n**Key points summarized:**\n\n- **Offensive penalty:** Every attack made against a *Poisoned* figure gets +1 Attack.\n- **Removal:** *Poison* is removed when the figure receives a *Heal* effect.\n- **Heal interaction:** Unlike other conditions removed by healing, *Poison* **blocks the hit point recovery** — the heal removes the condition but does not restore any HP.\n\n*Source: Frosthaven Rulebook, passage 101 (Negative Conditions)*",
