      "ok": true,
      "answer": "## Long Rests in Frosthaven\n\nHere's how long rests work, straight from the rulebook:\n\n**Declaring a Long Rest**\nDuring the **Card Selection** step, a character may declare a long rest instead of selecting two cards to play. This requires at least two cards in their *discard pile*. Their entire turn for the round is replaced by the long rest, and it is performed on **initiative 99**.\n\n**Steps of a Long Rest (in order):**\n\n1. **Lose one card of choice** from their discard pile and return the remaining discarded cards to their hand. *(mandatory)*\n2. **Perform \"*Heal* 2, self\"** *(optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items** *(optional)* — items can even be used during the same turn in which they are recovered.\n\n> \"When a character long rests, they follow these steps: Lose one card of their choice from their discard pile and return the remaining cards to their hand (mandatory). Perform 'Heal 2, self' (optional). Recover all of their spent items (optional). Items can be used during the same turn in which they are recovered.\"\n\n**Source:** Frosthaven Rulebook, p. 38",
